IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g6-interpretation`
IMPORT `g6-art15-16-deregistration`

-- g6-tests-art15-16.l4: tests of Articles 15 and 16 (Deregistration on application by entity; Deregistration in other cases).
-- Every expected value was decided from the text of the Law before the module was first run; the quotation above a group is the text it comes from.
-- A DEONTIC cannot be compared in #ASSERT, so duties and powers are exercised by #TRACE, each with its outcome in the `-- EXPECT:` comment above it
-- (read by work/g6/check-traces.py); the facts behind them are asserted on the BOOLEAN rules.

§ `Tests of Articles 15 and 16`

§§ `Article 15 -- Deregistration on application by entity`

-- src:430 | (1) An entity that is a registered charity may apply to the Commissioner to terminate the registration of the entity as a charity (to “deregister” the entity).
-- (1) An entity that is a registered charity may apply to the Commissioner to terminate the registration.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 15(1) the registered charity may apply to be deregistered` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a registered charity` DOES `apply to the Commissioner to terminate the registration` `a registered charity` AT 4
-- A permission not used is not a breach: it stands.
-- EXPECT: STANDING apply to the Commissioner to terminate the registration
#TRACE `Art 15(1) the registered charity may apply to be deregistered` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)
-- An entity that is not a registered charity has no such permission.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 15(1) the registered charity may apply to be deregistered` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)

-- src:431 | (2) An entity applying for deregistration must provide the Commissioner with any information or document requested by the Commissioner in relation to the entity’s proposals for the continuation or winding up of the entity and for the application of any of its property remaining after deregistration.
-- (2) An entity applying for deregistration must provide the Commissioner with any information or document requested by the Commissioner in relation to the entity's proposals.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 15(2) the entity must provide the information requested` TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a registered charity` DOES `provide the Commissioner with the information or document requested` `a registered charity` AT 20
-- No period is stated: the duty stands until it is done, however long it takes.
-- EXPECT: STANDING provide the Commissioner with the information or document requested
#TRACE `Art 15(2) the entity must provide the information requested` TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)
-- No application, or no request: the duty has not arisen.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 15(2) the entity must provide the information requested` FALSE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 15(2) the entity must provide the information requested` TRUE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)

-- src:432 | (3) If the entity complies with paragraph (2) the Commissioner must –
-- src:433 | (a) deregister the entity; or
-- src:434 | (b) refuse to deregister the entity on grounds relating to the proposals mentioned in paragraph (2).
-- (3) If the entity complies with paragraph (2) the Commissioner must (a) deregister the entity; or (b) refuse to deregister the entity on grounds relating to the proposals mentioned in paragraph (2).
-- Complied, grounds for refusal exist: either act discharges the duty.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 15(3) the Commissioner must deregister or refuse` `the readings taken` TRUE TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `deregister the entity` `the Commissioner` AT 9
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 15(3) the Commissioner must deregister or refuse` `the readings taken` TRUE TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `refuse to deregister the entity on grounds relating to the proposals` `the Commissioner` AT 9
-- EXPECT: STANDING deregister the entity
#TRACE `Art 15(3) the Commissioner must deregister or refuse` `the readings taken` TRUE TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)
-- Complied, and no grounds relating to the proposals: only deregistering is available; a refusal does not discharge the duty.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 15(3) the Commissioner must deregister or refuse` `the readings taken` TRUE TRUE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `deregister the entity` `the Commissioner` AT 9
-- EXPECT: STANDING deregister the entity
#TRACE `Art 15(3) the Commissioner must deregister or refuse` `the readings taken` TRUE TRUE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `refuse to deregister the entity on grounds relating to the proposals` `the Commissioner` AT 9
-- No application: no duty.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 15(3) the Commissioner must deregister or refuse` `the readings taken` FALSE TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)
-- F6.1: the entity supplies none of the information requested. Reading taken: the paragraph states no rule, so no duty arises under it.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 15(3) the Commissioner must deregister or refuse` `the readings taken` TRUE FALSE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)
-- The other readings of F6.1: the Commissioner may refuse (B), must refuse (C), the Law states no rule (D).
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 15(3) the Commissioner must deregister or refuse` (`the readings taken but with F6.1 read as` `the Commissioner may refuse to deregister`) TRUE FALSE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `refuse to deregister the entity because paragraph (2) has not been complied with` `the Commissioner` AT 9
-- EXPECT: STANDING refuse to deregister the entity because paragraph (2) has not been complied with
#TRACE `Art 15(3) the Commissioner must deregister or refuse` (`the readings taken but with F6.1 read as` `the Commissioner may refuse to deregister`) TRUE FALSE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 15(3) the Commissioner must deregister or refuse` (`the readings taken but with F6.1 read as` `the Commissioner must refuse to deregister`) TRUE FALSE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `refuse to deregister the entity because paragraph (2) has not been complied with` `the Commissioner` AT 9
-- EXPECT: STANDING MUST
#TRACE `Art 15(3) the Commissioner must deregister or refuse` (`the readings taken but with F6.1 read as` `the Commissioner must refuse to deregister`) TRUE FALSE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)
#ASSERT REFUSED `F6.1 reading D: the Law states no rule for an application where paragraph (2) has not been complied with`
#ASSERT REFUSED `Art 15(3) where the entity has not complied with paragraph (2)` (`the readings taken but with F6.1 read as` `the Law states no rule for that case`)
-- Reading D is reached only for an application whose entity has not complied: an entity that has complied is not touched by it.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 15(3) the Commissioner must deregister or refuse` (`the readings taken but with F6.1 read as` `the Law states no rule for that case`) TRUE TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `deregister the entity` `the Commissioner` AT 9
-- IP27: the decision under Article 15(3) is one decision, "whether to deregister on application", whose outcome is doing what was sought or refusing.
#ASSERT       `Art 15(3) the decision of the Commissioner` TRUE EQUALS `Decision of the Commissioner` OF `whether to deregister a charity on its own application, Article 15(3)`, `the Commissioner does what was sought or proposed`
#ASSERT       `Art 15(3) the decision of the Commissioner` FALSE EQUALS `Decision of the Commissioner` OF `whether to deregister a charity on its own application, Article 15(3)`, `the Commissioner refuses`

§§ `Article 16 -- Deregistration in other cases`

-- Positional construction of the preliminary notice of Article 16(1): given on; the last day for objections; in writing; specifies reasons; invites objections within a time it specifies; the time is reasonable.
`a complete notice given on 1 March 2026 inviting objections until 31 March 2026, the time reasonable` MEANS `Preliminary notice of Article 16(1)` OF (YMD 2026 3 1), (YMD 2026 3 31), TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE
`a complete notice given on 1 March 2026 inviting objections until 2 March 2026, the time not reasonable` MEANS `Preliminary notice of Article 16(1)` OF (YMD 2026 3 1), (YMD 2026 3 2), TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE
`a notice given on 1 March 2026 that is not in writing` MEANS `Preliminary notice of Article 16(1)` OF (YMD 2026 3 1), (YMD 2026 3 31), FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE
`a notice given on 1 March 2026 that specifies no reasons` MEANS `Preliminary notice of Article 16(1)` OF (YMD 2026 3 1), (YMD 2026 3 31), TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE
`a notice given on 1 March 2026 that invites no objections` MEANS `Preliminary notice of Article 16(1)` OF (YMD 2026 3 1), (YMD 2026 3 31), TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE

-- Positional construction of the other facts: the Commissioner was misled; a circumstance prescribed by Order applies; the Commissioner is satisfied that it is proportionate to deregister.
`no ground but the Commissioner is satisfied` MEANS `Facts about the grounds of Article 16(1)` OF FALSE, FALSE, TRUE
`the Commissioner was misled, and is satisfied` MEANS `Facts about the grounds of Article 16(1)` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE
`a prescribed circumstance applies, and the Commissioner is satisfied` MEANS `Facts about the grounds of Article 16(1)` OF FALSE, TRUE, TRUE
`the Commissioner was misled, but is not satisfied that deregistering is proportionate` MEANS `Facts about the grounds of Article 16(1)` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`no ground, and the Commissioner is not satisfied` MEANS `Facts about the grounds of Article 16(1)` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE

-- Required steps notices (IP19): served on; prompted by; date served; the end of the time named for the steps; requires a governor to be suspended or removed; has been complied with.
`a notice on the charity, steps due by 28 February 2026, not complied with` MEANS `Required steps notice` OF `the registered charity`, `there has been misconduct by a registered charity`, (YMD 2026 1 15), JUST (YMD 2026 2 28), FALSE, FALSE
`a notice on the charity, steps due by 31 December 2026, not complied with` MEANS `Required steps notice` OF `the registered charity`, `there has been misconduct by a registered charity`, (YMD 2026 1 15), JUST (YMD 2026 12 31), FALSE, FALSE
`a notice on a governor, steps due by 28 February 2026, not complied with` MEANS `Required steps notice` OF `a governor of the registered charity`, `a governor of a registered charity has engaged in misconduct`, (YMD 2026 1 15), JUST (YMD 2026 2 28), FALSE, FALSE
`a notice on the charity, steps due by 28 February 2026, complied with` MEANS `Required steps notice` OF `the registered charity`, `there has been misconduct by a registered charity`, (YMD 2026 1 15), JUST (YMD 2026 2 28), FALSE, TRUE
`a notice on the charity, no time named, not complied with` MEANS `Required steps notice` OF `the registered charity`, `a registered charity does not pass the charity test`, (YMD 2026 1 15), NOTHING, FALSE, FALSE

§§§ `Article 16(1) -- the grounds`

-- src:437 | (a) the entity no longer meets the charity test;
-- (a) the entity no longer meets the charity test.
#ASSERT       `Art 16(1)(a) the entity no longer meets the charity test` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 16(1)(a) the entity no longer meets the charity test` TRUE
-- src:438 | (b) the Commissioner was misled into registering the entity, whether by the entity or by any other person and whether intentionally or otherwise;
-- (b) the Commissioner was misled into registering the entity, whether by the entity or by any other person and whether intentionally or otherwise.
#ASSERT       `Art 16(1)(b) the Commissioner was misled into registering the entity` `the Commissioner was misled, and is satisfied`
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 16(1)(b) the Commissioner was misled into registering the entity` `no ground but the Commissioner is satisfied`
-- src:439 | (c) the entity has failed to comply with a required steps notice; or
-- (c) the entity has failed to comply with a required steps notice. F6.19: with the steps due by 28 February 2026, the entity has failed on 1 March; not on 28 February itself.
#ASSERT       `Art 16(1)(c) the entity has failed to comply with a required steps notice` `the readings taken` (LIST `a notice on the charity, steps due by 28 February 2026, not complied with`) (YMD 2026 3 1)
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 16(1)(c) the entity has failed to comply with a required steps notice` `the readings taken` (LIST `a notice on the charity, steps due by 28 February 2026, not complied with`) (YMD 2026 2 28)
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 16(1)(c) the entity has failed to comply with a required steps notice` `the readings taken` (LIST `a notice on the charity, steps due by 28 February 2026, not complied with`) (YMD 2026 2 27)
-- The other reading: any notice whose steps have not been taken, whenever the time. The discriminating case: a notice due next December, asked in March.
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 16(1)(c) the entity has failed to comply with a required steps notice` `the readings taken` (LIST `a notice on the charity, steps due by 31 December 2026, not complied with`) (YMD 2026 3 1)
#ASSERT       `Art 16(1)(c) the entity has failed to comply with a required steps notice` (`the readings taken but with F6.19 read as` `the notice has not been complied with whenever the steps have not yet been taken`) (LIST `a notice on the charity, steps due by 31 December 2026, not complied with`) (YMD 2026 3 1)
#ASSERT       `Art 16(1)(c) the entity has failed to comply with a required steps notice` (`the readings taken but with F6.19 read as` `the notice has not been complied with whenever the steps have not yet been taken`) (LIST `a notice on the charity, steps due by 28 February 2026, not complied with`) (YMD 2026 2 27)
-- A notice on a governor is not the entity's; a notice complied with is not failed; a notice that names no time can be failed as soon as the steps are not taken; no notice, no failure.
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 16(1)(c) the entity has failed to comply with a required steps notice` `the readings taken` (LIST `a notice on a governor, steps due by 28 February 2026, not complied with`) (YMD 2026 3 1)
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 16(1)(c) the entity has failed to comply with a required steps notice` (`the readings taken but with F6.19 read as` `the notice has not been complied with whenever the steps have not yet been taken`) (LIST `a notice on a governor, steps due by 28 February 2026, not complied with`) (YMD 2026 3 1)
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 16(1)(c) the entity has failed to comply with a required steps notice` `the readings taken` (LIST `a notice on the charity, steps due by 28 February 2026, complied with`) (YMD 2026 3 1)
#ASSERT       `Art 16(1)(c) the entity has failed to comply with a required steps notice` `the readings taken` (LIST `a notice on the charity, no time named, not complied with`) (YMD 2026 3 1)
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 16(1)(c) the entity has failed to comply with a required steps notice` `the readings taken` EMPTY (YMD 2026 3 1)
-- One failed notice among several is enough.
#ASSERT       `Art 16(1)(c) the entity has failed to comply with a required steps notice` `the readings taken` (LIST `a notice on the charity, steps due by 28 February 2026, complied with`, `a notice on the charity, steps due by 28 February 2026, not complied with`) (YMD 2026 3 1)
-- src:440 | (d) any other circumstance prescribed by the Minister by Order applies.
-- (d) any other circumstance prescribed by the Minister by Order applies.
#ASSERT       `Art 16(1)(d) a circumstance prescribed by the Minister by Order applies` `a prescribed circumstance applies, and the Commissioner is satisfied`
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 16(1)(d) a circumstance prescribed by the Minister by Order applies` `the Commissioner was misled, and is satisfied`
-- The power of the Minister to prescribe.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 16(1)(d) the Minister may prescribe a circumstance of deregistration by Order` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `prescribe by Order a circumstance in which the entity is deregistered` `the Minister` AT 10
-- EXPECT: STANDING prescribe by Order a circumstance in which the entity is deregistered
#TRACE `Art 16(1)(d) the Minister may prescribe a circumstance of deregistration by Order` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)
-- src:436 | (1) The Commissioner may, by written notice to an entity that is registered as a charity, deregister the entity if satisfied, after giving the entity written notice specifying reasons and inviting objections within a reasonable time specified in the notice, that it is proportionate to do so on the ground that –
-- src:437 | (a) the entity no longer meets the charity test;
-- src:438 | (b) the Commissioner was misled into registering the entity, whether by the entity or by any other person and whether intentionally or otherwise;
-- src:439 | (c) the entity has failed to comply with a required steps notice; or
-- src:440 | (d) any other circumstance prescribed by the Minister by Order applies.
-- Some ground exists if any of (a) to (d) does.
#ASSERT       `Art 16(1) a ground of Article 16(1) exists` `the readings taken` FALSE EMPTY `no ground but the Commissioner is satisfied` (YMD 2026 4 1)
#ASSERT       `Art 16(1) a ground of Article 16(1) exists` `the readings taken` TRUE EMPTY `the Commissioner was misled, and is satisfied` (YMD 2026 4 1)
#ASSERT       `Art 16(1) a ground of Article 16(1) exists` `the readings taken` TRUE (LIST `a notice on the charity, steps due by 28 February 2026, not complied with`) `no ground but the Commissioner is satisfied` (YMD 2026 4 1)
#ASSERT       `Art 16(1) a ground of Article 16(1) exists` `the readings taken` TRUE EMPTY `a prescribed circumstance applies, and the Commissioner is satisfied` (YMD 2026 4 1)
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 16(1) a ground of Article 16(1) exists` `the readings taken` TRUE EMPTY `no ground but the Commissioner is satisfied` (YMD 2026 4 1)

§§§ `Article 16(1) -- the preliminary notice and its time`

-- src:436 | (1) The Commissioner may, by written notice to an entity that is registered as a charity, deregister the entity if satisfied, after giving the entity written notice specifying reasons and inviting objections within a reasonable time specified in the notice, that it is proportionate to do so on the ground that –
-- "after giving the entity written notice specifying reasons and inviting objections within a reasonable time specified in the notice": the notice has its three formal parts, and (F6.13) the time is reasonable.
#ASSERT       `Art 16(1) the preliminary notice is the notice the paragraph requires` `the readings taken` `a complete notice given on 1 March 2026 inviting objections until 31 March 2026, the time reasonable`
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 16(1) the preliminary notice is the notice the paragraph requires` `the readings taken` `a complete notice given on 1 March 2026 inviting objections until 2 March 2026, the time not reasonable`
#ASSERT       `Art 16(1) the preliminary notice is the notice the paragraph requires` (`the readings taken but with F6.13 read as` `any time specified suffices`) `a complete notice given on 1 March 2026 inviting objections until 2 March 2026, the time not reasonable`
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 16(1) the preliminary notice is the notice the paragraph requires` `the readings taken` `a notice given on 1 March 2026 that is not in writing`
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 16(1) the preliminary notice is the notice the paragraph requires` `the readings taken` `a notice given on 1 March 2026 that specifies no reasons`
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 16(1) the preliminary notice is the notice the paragraph requires` `the readings taken` `a notice given on 1 March 2026 that invites no objections`
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 16(1) the preliminary notice is the notice the paragraph requires` (`the readings taken but with F6.13 read as` `any time specified suffices`) `a notice given on 1 March 2026 that is not in writing`
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 16(1) the preliminary notice is the notice the paragraph requires` (`the readings taken but with F6.13 read as` `any time specified suffices`) `a notice given on 1 March 2026 that specifies no reasons`
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 16(1) the preliminary notice is the notice the paragraph requires` (`the readings taken but with F6.13 read as` `any time specified suffices`) `a notice given on 1 March 2026 that invites no objections`
-- F6.17: given on 1 March, objections invited until 31 March. May the Commissioner deregister at any time after giving the notice (A), only after 31 March (the reading taken), only on or after 31 March (C)?
#ASSERT       `Art 16(1) the time for objections allows deregistration on the day` (`the readings taken but with F6.17 read as` `the Commissioner may deregister at any time after the notice is given`) `a complete notice given on 1 March 2026 inviting objections until 31 March 2026, the time reasonable` (YMD 2026 3 15)
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 16(1) the time for objections allows deregistration on the day` `the readings taken` `a complete notice given on 1 March 2026 inviting objections until 31 March 2026, the time reasonable` (YMD 2026 3 15)
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 16(1) the time for objections allows deregistration on the day` `the readings taken` `a complete notice given on 1 March 2026 inviting objections until 31 March 2026, the time reasonable` (YMD 2026 3 31)
#ASSERT       `Art 16(1) the time for objections allows deregistration on the day` `the readings taken` `a complete notice given on 1 March 2026 inviting objections until 31 March 2026, the time reasonable` (YMD 2026 4 1)
#ASSERT       `Art 16(1) the time for objections allows deregistration on the day` (`the readings taken but with F6.17 read as` `the Commissioner may deregister only on or after the last day for objections`) `a complete notice given on 1 March 2026 inviting objections until 31 March 2026, the time reasonable` (YMD 2026 3 31)
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 16(1) the time for objections allows deregistration on the day` (`the readings taken but with F6.17 read as` `the Commissioner may deregister only on or after the last day for objections`) `a complete notice given on 1 March 2026 inviting objections until 31 March 2026, the time reasonable` (YMD 2026 3 30)
-- Before the notice was given, no reading allows it.
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 16(1) the time for objections allows deregistration on the day` (`the readings taken but with F6.17 read as` `the Commissioner may deregister at any time after the notice is given`) `a complete notice given on 1 March 2026 inviting objections until 31 March 2026, the time reasonable` (YMD 2026 2 28)
-- The day the notice is given: allowed on the first reading (a date has no hour), not on the others.
#ASSERT       `Art 16(1) the time for objections allows deregistration on the day` (`the readings taken but with F6.17 read as` `the Commissioner may deregister at any time after the notice is given`) `a complete notice given on 1 March 2026 inviting objections until 31 March 2026, the time reasonable` (YMD 2026 3 1)
-- No notice, no procedure followed.
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 16(1) the procedure of the preliminary notice has been followed by the day` `the readings taken` NOTHING (YMD 2026 4 1)
#ASSERT       `Art 16(1) the procedure of the preliminary notice has been followed by the day` `the readings taken` (JUST `a complete notice given on 1 March 2026 inviting objections until 31 March 2026, the time reasonable`) (YMD 2026 4 1)

-- src:436 | (1) The Commissioner may, by written notice to an entity that is registered as a charity, deregister the entity if satisfied, after giving the entity written notice specifying reasons and inviting objections within a reasonable time specified in the notice, that it is proportionate to do so on the ground that –
-- The power. Registered, a ground (a: the entity no longer meets the charity test), the Commissioner satisfied, a good preliminary notice that has run its time: the Commissioner may deregister by written notice.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 16(1) the Commissioner may deregister the entity` `the readings taken` TRUE FALSE EMPTY `no ground but the Commissioner is satisfied` (JUST `a complete notice given on 1 March 2026 inviting objections until 31 March 2026, the time reasonable`) (YMD 2026 4 1) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `deregister the entity by written notice` `the Commissioner` AT 9
-- A power not used stands.
-- EXPECT: STANDING deregister the entity by written notice
#TRACE `Art 16(1) the Commissioner may deregister the entity` `the readings taken` TRUE FALSE EMPTY `no ground but the Commissioner is satisfied` (JUST `a complete notice given on 1 March 2026 inviting objections until 31 March 2026, the time reasonable`) (YMD 2026 4 1) AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)
-- Each other ground suffices: (b) misled; (c) failed to comply; (d) a prescribed circumstance.
-- EXPECT: STANDING deregister the entity by written notice
#TRACE `Art 16(1) the Commissioner may deregister the entity` `the readings taken` TRUE TRUE EMPTY `the Commissioner was misled, and is satisfied` (JUST `a complete notice given on 1 March 2026 inviting objections until 31 March 2026, the time reasonable`) (YMD 2026 4 1) AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)
-- EXPECT: STANDING deregister the entity by written notice
#TRACE `Art 16(1) the Commissioner may deregister the entity` `the readings taken` TRUE TRUE (LIST `a notice on the charity, steps due by 28 February 2026, not complied with`) `no ground but the Commissioner is satisfied` (JUST `a complete notice given on 1 March 2026 inviting objections until 31 March 2026, the time reasonable`) (YMD 2026 4 1) AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)
-- EXPECT: STANDING deregister the entity by written notice
#TRACE `Art 16(1) the Commissioner may deregister the entity` `the readings taken` TRUE TRUE EMPTY `a prescribed circumstance applies, and the Commissioner is satisfied` (JUST `a complete notice given on 1 March 2026 inviting objections until 31 March 2026, the time reasonable`) (YMD 2026 4 1) AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)
-- No power without each condition: not a registered charity; no ground; not satisfied; no preliminary notice; the time for objections not run; an unreasonable time.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 16(1) the Commissioner may deregister the entity` `the readings taken` FALSE FALSE EMPTY `no ground but the Commissioner is satisfied` (JUST `a complete notice given on 1 March 2026 inviting objections until 31 March 2026, the time reasonable`) (YMD 2026 4 1) AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 16(1) the Commissioner may deregister the entity` `the readings taken` TRUE TRUE EMPTY `no ground but the Commissioner is satisfied` (JUST `a complete notice given on 1 March 2026 inviting objections until 31 March 2026, the time reasonable`) (YMD 2026 4 1) AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 16(1) the Commissioner may deregister the entity` `the readings taken` TRUE FALSE EMPTY `the Commissioner was misled, but is not satisfied that deregistering is proportionate` (JUST `a complete notice given on 1 March 2026 inviting objections until 31 March 2026, the time reasonable`) (YMD 2026 4 1) AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 16(1) the Commissioner may deregister the entity` `the readings taken` TRUE FALSE EMPTY `the Commissioner was misled, and is satisfied` NOTHING (YMD 2026 4 1) AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 16(1) the Commissioner may deregister the entity` `the readings taken` TRUE FALSE EMPTY `the Commissioner was misled, and is satisfied` (JUST `a complete notice given on 1 March 2026 inviting objections until 31 March 2026, the time reasonable`) (YMD 2026 3 15) AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)
-- ... but on the F6.17 reading that lets the Commissioner deregister at any time after the notice, the same facts give the power.
-- EXPECT: STANDING deregister the entity by written notice
#TRACE `Art 16(1) the Commissioner may deregister the entity` (`the readings taken but with F6.17 read as` `the Commissioner may deregister at any time after the notice is given`) TRUE FALSE EMPTY `the Commissioner was misled, and is satisfied` (JUST `a complete notice given on 1 March 2026 inviting objections until 31 March 2026, the time reasonable`) (YMD 2026 3 15) AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)
-- F6.13: a notice that gives one day (an unreasonable time). Not a power on the reading taken; a power if any time specified suffices.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 16(1) the Commissioner may deregister the entity` `the readings taken` TRUE FALSE EMPTY `the Commissioner was misled, and is satisfied` (JUST `a complete notice given on 1 March 2026 inviting objections until 2 March 2026, the time not reasonable`) (YMD 2026 4 1) AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)
-- EXPECT: STANDING deregister the entity by written notice
#TRACE `Art 16(1) the Commissioner may deregister the entity` (`the readings taken but with F6.13 read as` `any time specified suffices`) TRUE FALSE EMPTY `the Commissioner was misled, and is satisfied` (JUST `a complete notice given on 1 March 2026 inviting objections until 2 March 2026, the time not reasonable`) (YMD 2026 4 1) AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)

§§§ `Article 16(2) -- the Commissioner must deregister an entity that no longer exists`

-- src:441 | (2) If the Commissioner is satisfied that an entity that is registered as a charity no longer exists, the Commissioner must, by written notice to any person purporting to be a governor of the entity or to be responsible for the winding up of the affairs of the entity, deregister the entity.
-- (2) If the Commissioner is satisfied that an entity that is registered as a charity no longer exists, the Commissioner must, by written notice ..., deregister the entity.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 16(2) the Commissioner must deregister the entity that no longer exists` `the readings taken` TRUE TRUE NOTHING (YMD 2026 4 1) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `deregister the entity by written notice` `the Commissioner` AT 9
-- No period is stated: the duty stands until it is done.
-- EXPECT: STANDING deregister the entity by written notice
#TRACE `Art 16(2) the Commissioner must deregister the entity that no longer exists` `the readings taken` TRUE TRUE NOTHING (YMD 2026 4 1) AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)
-- Not satisfied that it no longer exists, or not a registered charity: no duty.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 16(2) the Commissioner must deregister the entity that no longer exists` `the readings taken` TRUE FALSE NOTHING (YMD 2026 4 1) AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 16(2) the Commissioner must deregister the entity that no longer exists` `the readings taken` FALSE TRUE NOTHING (YMD 2026 4 1) AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)
-- F6.2, the discriminating case: an entity that has ceased to exist and also fails the charity test; no preliminary notice has been given. 16(2) governs alone on the reading taken: the Commissioner must deregister.
-- The 16(1) power, in the same case, is not available (no preliminary notice).
-- EXPECT: STANDING deregister the entity by written notice
#TRACE `Art 16(2) the Commissioner must deregister the entity that no longer exists` `the readings taken` TRUE TRUE NOTHING (YMD 2026 4 1) AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 16(1) the Commissioner may deregister the entity` `the readings taken` TRUE FALSE EMPTY `no ground but the Commissioner is satisfied` NOTHING (YMD 2026 4 1) AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)
-- On the other reading, 16(2) follows the procedure of 16(1): with no preliminary notice nothing is owed yet; with a good notice that has run its time, the duty arises.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 16(2) the Commissioner must deregister the entity that no longer exists` (`the readings taken but with F6.2 read as` `Article 16(2) follows the procedure of Article 16(1) and the duty arises only after the prior notice has run its time`) TRUE TRUE NOTHING (YMD 2026 4 1) AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)
-- EXPECT: STANDING deregister the entity by written notice
#TRACE `Art 16(2) the Commissioner must deregister the entity that no longer exists` (`the readings taken but with F6.2 read as` `Article 16(2) follows the procedure of Article 16(1) and the duty arises only after the prior notice has run its time`) TRUE TRUE (JUST `a complete notice given on 1 March 2026 inviting objections until 31 March 2026, the time reasonable`) (YMD 2026 4 1) AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 16(2) the Commissioner must deregister the entity that no longer exists` (`the readings taken but with F6.2 read as` `Article 16(2) follows the procedure of Article 16(1) and the duty arises only after the prior notice has run its time`) TRUE TRUE (JUST `a complete notice given on 1 March 2026 inviting objections until 31 March 2026, the time reasonable`) (YMD 2026 3 15) AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)

-- IP27: the decision of the Commissioner under Article 16.
#ASSERT       `Art 16 the decision of the Commissioner` TRUE EQUALS `Decision of the Commissioner` OF `whether to deregister a charity in other cases, Article 16`, `the Commissioner does what was sought or proposed`
#ASSERT       `Art 16 the decision of the Commissioner` FALSE EQUALS `Decision of the Commissioner` OF `whether to deregister a charity in other cases, Article 16`, `the Commissioner refuses`

§§ `Articles 15 and 16 -- why the entity was deregistered (IP32)`

-- src:433 | (a) deregister the entity; or
-- src:437 | (a) the entity no longer meets the charity test;
-- src:438 | (b) the Commissioner was misled into registering the entity, whether by the entity or by any other person and whether intentionally or otherwise;
-- src:439 | (c) the entity has failed to comply with a required steps notice; or
-- src:440 | (d) any other circumstance prescribed by the Minister by Order applies.
-- src:441 | (2) If the Commissioner is satisfied that an entity that is registered as a charity no longer exists, the Commissioner must, by written notice to any person purporting to be a governor of the entity or to be responsible for the winding up of the affairs of the entity, deregister the entity.
#ASSERT       `Art 16 the basis of deregistration` `on the entity's own application under Article 15(3)(a)` EQUALS `on the entity's own application under Article 15`
#ASSERT       `Art 16 the basis of deregistration` `by written notice under Article 16(1) on the ground that the entity no longer meets the charity test` EQUALS `the entity no longer meets the charity test`
#ASSERT       `Art 16 the basis of deregistration` `by written notice under Article 16(1) on the ground that the Commissioner was misled into registering the entity` EQUALS `the Commissioner was misled into registering the entity`
#ASSERT       `Art 16 the basis of deregistration` `by written notice under Article 16(1) on the ground that the entity has failed to comply with a required steps notice` EQUALS `the entity has failed to comply with a required steps notice`
#ASSERT       `Art 16 the basis of deregistration` `by written notice under Article 16(1) on a circumstance prescribed by Order` EQUALS `a circumstance prescribed by Order under Article 16(1)(d)`
#ASSERT       `Art 16 the basis of deregistration` `by written notice under Article 16(2) because the entity no longer exists` EQUALS `the entity no longer exists`
-- The ground relied on exists on the facts: ground (a) when the entity does not meet the charity test; (b) when the Commissioner was misled; (c) when a notice has been failed; (d) when a prescribed circumstance applies.
#ASSERT       `Art 16(1) the ground relied on exists` `the readings taken` `by written notice under Article 16(1) on the ground that the entity no longer meets the charity test` FALSE EMPTY `no ground but the Commissioner is satisfied` (YMD 2026 4 1)
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 16(1) the ground relied on exists` `the readings taken` `by written notice under Article 16(1) on the ground that the entity no longer meets the charity test` TRUE EMPTY `no ground but the Commissioner is satisfied` (YMD 2026 4 1)
#ASSERT       `Art 16(1) the ground relied on exists` `the readings taken` `by written notice under Article 16(1) on the ground that the Commissioner was misled into registering the entity` TRUE EMPTY `the Commissioner was misled, and is satisfied` (YMD 2026 4 1)
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 16(1) the ground relied on exists` `the readings taken` `by written notice under Article 16(1) on the ground that the Commissioner was misled into registering the entity` TRUE EMPTY `no ground but the Commissioner is satisfied` (YMD 2026 4 1)
#ASSERT       `Art 16(1) the ground relied on exists` `the readings taken` `by written notice under Article 16(1) on the ground that the entity has failed to comply with a required steps notice` TRUE (LIST `a notice on the charity, steps due by 28 February 2026, not complied with`) `no ground but the Commissioner is satisfied` (YMD 2026 4 1)
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 16(1) the ground relied on exists` `the readings taken` `by written notice under Article 16(1) on the ground that the entity has failed to comply with a required steps notice` TRUE EMPTY `no ground but the Commissioner is satisfied` (YMD 2026 4 1)
#ASSERT       `Art 16(1) the ground relied on exists` `the readings taken` `by written notice under Article 16(1) on a circumstance prescribed by Order` TRUE EMPTY `a prescribed circumstance applies, and the Commissioner is satisfied` (YMD 2026 4 1)
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 16(1) the ground relied on exists` `the readings taken` `by written notice under Article 16(1) on a circumstance prescribed by Order` TRUE EMPTY `no ground but the Commissioner is satisfied` (YMD 2026 4 1)
-- A deregistration on the entity's own application, or because it no longer exists, relies on no ground of Article 16(1): nothing further is asked.
#ASSERT       `Art 16(1) the ground relied on exists` `the readings taken` `on the entity's own application under Article 15(3)(a)` TRUE EMPTY `no ground but the Commissioner is satisfied` (YMD 2026 4 1)
#ASSERT       `Art 16(1) the ground relied on exists` `the readings taken` `by written notice under Article 16(2) because the entity no longer exists` TRUE EMPTY `no ground but the Commissioner is satisfied` (YMD 2026 4 1)
